<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       NO GLITTERHEARTS ON THE GROUND

       Ushanka's surface sites are two heart sources, and both have to close
       or the orbital gate is decorative.

       1. USH_Glittercrate opens into USH_RewardGlittercrate, whose first
          RandomOption is a weight-0.5 glitterheart - the single most likely
          outcome. Weight goes to 0 rather than deleting the node: a
          RandomOption never selects a zero-weight entry, the structure stays
          intact, and reverting is a one-character change. The crate's other
          options (plasteel, and the rest of the table) are untouched, so
          surface sites stay worth clearing.

       2. The KCSG symbol USH_GlittershipChunk places a real chunk in their
          surface layouts, and a chunk deconstructs into 3 hearts. Rather
          than editing KCSG layout strings - fragile, and hundreds of cells -
          the SYMBOL is repointed at plain slag. Surface sites still show
          wreckage; the wreckage just is not glitterworld any more.

          The real USH_GlittershipChunk ThingDef is untouched, so the
          orbital prefab (Archinity_GlittershipDebris) still places the
          genuine article. Chunks become an orbit-only thing, which is where
          a piece of a glittership should have been all along.

       Net: surface glitter sites remain husks worth raiding for plasteel,
       components and their normal loot table. They stop being a heart farm.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Ushankas Glittertech Expansion</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- 1. Crates no longer roll hearts. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingSetMakerDef[defName="USH_RewardGlittercrate"]//li[thingSetMaker/fixedParams/filter/thingDefs/li="USH_Glitterheart"]/weight</xpath>
          <value>
            <weight>0</weight>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- 2. Surface wreckage is ordinary slag, not glitterworld debris. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/KCSG.SymbolDef[defName="USH_GlittershipChunk"]/thing</xpath>
          <value>
            <thing>ChunkSlagSteel</thing>
          </value>
        </li>
        <!-- USH_GlittershipChunk_North is NOT a def - KCSG generates rotation
             variants at runtime from the ThingDef, so it cannot be patched.
             The layout references it directly in exactly one row, so that row
             is rewritten instead. Only one line in 649 contains it. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>//li[text()="HiddenConduit,.,.,.,.,USH_GlittershipChunk_North,.,.,AncientRazorWire,.,HiddenConduit"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>HiddenConduit,.,.,.,.,ChunkSlagSteel,.,.,AncientRazorWire,.,HiddenConduit</li>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
